{
  "about": [
    "Design section 7.1's dependency gate (B4 recheck 6 item 2; rebuilt for the B7 milestone 2",
    "break-it, HIGH-1, MEDIUM-1 and LOW-1). Every direct dependency of every workspace crate",
    "(normal, build and dev) has a reviewed entry under `dependencies`: its `kind` (runtime,",
    "build-only or dev-only, checked against the manifests and the Cargo.lock graph), its",
    "`capability` (`none`, or a set of filesystem, process, signals, syscalls, network) and why.",
    "A destructive-capable category (filesystem, process, signals, syscalls) lists its",
    "`destructive` paths, each disallowed in clippy.toml, or records in `no_destructive_api` why",
    "its API has none (never for a raw system-call crate). Cargo.lock can only require more: a",
    "raw system-call crate underneath a `none` dependency needs a `raw_use` reason. Packages that",
    "can wrap system calls without being direct are named under `transitive`.",
    "proven::tests::dependency_gate checks all of it, and two backstops for a mistaken `none`:",
    "production code naming a destructive-looking function through a dependency's path that",
    "clippy.toml does not disallow, and a `none`, `network` or no-destructive-API dependency",
    "whose own locked source reaches a std, Tokio or libc path clippy.toml disallows. std is",
    "the toolchain's, gated by its clippy.toml paths directly (a curated review in the same test)."
  ],
